{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "Quick action reference",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C1",
      "text": "- Start by searching a people-search site for your name or other identifying information such as a phone number or address.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C2",
      "text": "- When you find a report about yourself, locate the site's opt-out or removal instructions and follow them.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C3",
      "text": "- Repeat the opt-out process across other relevant people-search sites; doing this one by one can be time-consuming.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limits and follow-up",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C4",
      "text": "- Periodically recheck people-search sites and submit new opt-out requests if your information reappears.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C5",
      "text": "- Opting out of people-search sites does not delete information from public records, so the workflow reduces exposure rather than guaranteeing total deletion.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C6",
      "text": "- Consumers can perform people-search opt-outs themselves for free or pay a service to perform the work on their behalf.",
      "type": "bullet"
    }
  ],
